  "text": "According to Newton's first law, an object will continue to move at a constant velocity unless acted upon by an external net force. This means that uniform motion, which is motion at a constant speed in a straight line, will only change if a net force is applied. For example, if you're riding a bicycle at a steady speed on a straight road, you're maintaining uniform motion. However, if you suddenly hit the brakes, the force of friction between the brake pads and the wheels acts as an external net force, causing you to slow down and stop. This change in motion is due to the force of friction, which is an external force that disrupts the uniform motion.",
